PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The consensus decisively supports Choice B as the only biologically and technically consistent explanation. In image-enabled sorting, cells are imaged upstream of droplet break-off; fragile, non-specific cell doublets readily dissociate under hydrodynamic shear forces, causing only one cell (typically the tumor cell) to be deposited into the well. Choice E is biochemically invalid because picograms of tumor cell RNA cannot saturate SuperScript III reverse transcriptase, which operates efficiently up to microgram levels. Choices C and D are ruled out due to prompt contradictions regarding doublet sorting yield and incorrect references to T-cell receptor chains.
}

